menu "XBee telemetry link"

    choice TELEMETRY_XBEE_MODE
        prompt "XBee serial mode"
        default TELEMETRY_XBEE_API
        help
            How the flight computer talks to the XBee over the UART. This
            must match the AP setting stored IN THE MODULE (set it with
            XCTU). The firmware never changes AP itself.

            This is the VEHICLE radio only. The ground radio can be in
            either mode, independently: the RF bytes on the air are the
            same. Tell the ground station which (--transparent, or the
            "transparent radio" box).

        config TELEMETRY_XBEE_API
            bool "API mode (AP=1) -- normal"
            help
                Every packet goes out in a 0x10 frame and every uplink
                command arrives in a 0x90 frame. Gives the boot-time ATVR
                check, the once-a-second ATDB uplink RSSI, and delivery
                status for unicast packets.

        config TELEMETRY_XBEE_TRANSPARENT
            bool "Transparent mode (AP=0) -- backup"
            help
                The packets are written to the UART as plain bytes and the
                module sends them to its stored destination (DH/DL; the
                factory default is broadcast). Uplink packets are found in
                the incoming byte stream by their magic byte, length and
                CRC.

                What you lose: the uplink RSSI field reads 0 (unknown), no
                delivery status, so no firmware retries (the radio's own
                MAC retries still apply), and the destination comes from
                the module, not the firmware. Packet format, commands and
                config upload are unchanged.

                Module settings (XCTU): AP=0, BD=115200 (or whatever this
                board uses), DH/DL = the ground radio or broadcast, and
                leave RO (packetization timeout) at its default.
    endchoice

    config TELEMETRY_XBEE_TRANSPARENT_VERIFY
        bool "Check the radio at boot with +++ / ATVR"
        depends on TELEMETRY_XBEE_TRANSPARENT
        default y
        help
            Enters command mode once at boot (guard time, +++, ATVR, ATDH,
            ATDL, ATCN) to prove a radio is there and log where it will
            send. Costs about 2.5 s of boot time. Without it the radio is
            reported as unverified (STATUS_FLAG_TELEM_OK clear) and
            telemetry is sent blind.

    config TELEMETRY_XBEE_GUARD_MS
        int "Command-mode guard time (ms)"
        depends on TELEMETRY_XBEE_TRANSPARENT_VERIFY
        range 100 5000
        default 1100
        help
            Silence held before and after +++. Must be LONGER than the
            module's GT setting (default 1000 ms). If you shorten GT in
            XCTU, you can shorten this to match and save boot time.

endmenu
